2025-05-01 03:08:49 - Thread-1212 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant tables / columns

• ball_by_ball  
  – match_id: join key to every delivery in a match  
  – over_id / ball_id / innings_no: finer‑grain join keys that, together with match_id, uniquely identify a ball  
  – striker: player (batsman) who faced that ball – the person whose runs we must total  

• batsman_scored  
  – match_id / over_id / ball_id / innings_no: same four‑column key as ball_by_ball, used to join  
  – runs_scored: runs credited to the striker off that particular ball  

• player  
  – player_id: primary key, equals ball_by_ball.striker  
  – player_name: optional, for readable output  

Typical condition we will need  
JOIN ball_by_ball b USING(match_id, over_id, ball_id, innings_no)  
JOIN batsman_scored s USING(match_id, over_id, ball_id, innings_no)  

Group by (b.match_id, b.striker) to get the total runs that every striker scores in each match, then test HAVING SUM(s.runs_scored) > 50.  
The final requested value is the overall average of those individual “50‑plus” totals.

Ten exploratory → complex queries
(Every query returns at most 20 rows, all names/columns wrapped in double quotes, each followed by a short description.)

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at the raw runs that are stored in batsman_scored.
SELECT *
FROM "batsman_scored"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show 20 distinct match_id values that have batsman_scored data.
SELECT DISTINCT "match_id"
FROM "batsman_scored"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Display how ball_by_ball identifies the striker for each ball.
SELECT "match_id", "over_id", "ball_id", "innings_no", "striker"
FROM "ball_by_ball"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Join the two granular tables to see striker + runs for each ball.
SELECT b."match_id", b."over_id", b."ball_id", b."innings_no",
       b."striker", s."runs_scored"
FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS b
JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS s
       USING ("match_id", "over_id", "ball_id", "innings_no")
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Compute total runs scored by each striker in each match (first 20).
SELECT b."match_id",
       b."striker"      AS "player_id",
       SUM(s."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS b
JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS s
       USING ("match_id", "over_id", "ball_id", "innings_no")
GROUP  BY b."match_id", b."striker"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Filter the previous result to show only 50+ totals.
SELECT b."match_id",
       b."striker"      AS "player_id",
       SUM(s."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS b
JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS s
       USING ("match_id", "over_id", "ball_id", "innings_no")
GROUP  BY b."match_id", b."striker"
HAVING SUM(s."runs_scored") > 50
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Attach the player’s name for readability (first 20 rows).
SELECT p."player_name",
       t50."match_id",
       t50."total_runs"
FROM  (
        SELECT b."match_id", b."striker" AS "player_id",
               SUM(s."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
        FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS b
        JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS s
               USING ("match_id", "over_id", "ball_id", "innings_no")
        GROUP  BY b."match_id", b."striker"
        HAVING SUM(s."runs_scored") > 50
      ) AS t50
JOIN  "player" AS p
      ON p."player_id" = t50."player_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Count how many individual (match, striker) 50+ scores exist.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "num_50_plus_entries"
FROM  (
        SELECT b."match_id", b."striker"
        FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS b
        JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS s
               USING ("match_id", "over_id", "ball_id", "innings_no")
        GROUP  BY b."match_id", b."striker"
        HAVING SUM(s."runs_scored") > 50
      ) AS t;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Sum all those qualifying totals to prepare for an average.
SELECT SUM(t50."total_runs") AS "sum_of_totals"
FROM  (
        SELECT b."match_id", b."striker",
               SUM(s."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
        FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS b
        JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS s
               USING ("match_id", "over_id", "ball_id", "innings_no")
        GROUP  BY b."match_id", b."striker"
        HAVING SUM(s."runs_scored") > 50
      ) AS t50;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL ANSWER – average of the total runs for every striker‑match where the striker scored > 50.
SELECT AVG(t50."total_runs")  AS "average_runs_for_50_plus"
FROM (
        SELECT b."match_id",
               b."striker",
               SUM(s."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
        FROM   "ball_by_ball"  AS b
        JOIN   "batsman_scored" AS s
               USING ("match_id", "over_id", "ball_id", "innings_no")
        GROUP  BY b."match_id", b."striker"
        HAVING SUM(s."runs_scored") > 50
     ) AS t50;
```

